 (namespace folder)←EstablishProject y;list;bool;type
⍝ If `y` is empty:
⍝  * In case of a single open Cider or acre project its project path is taken.
⍝  * If there are several Cider/acre projects open then the user will be prompted.\\
⍝ Otherwise `y` must be the name of an open Cider/acre project or a path to a project.\\
⍝ Returns a two-element vector with a namespace name and folder, possibly both empty.\\
⍝ In case a path is specified it does not have to be an opened Cider/acre project. However, this will effect only a few
⍝ commands (like `IsDirty`, `OpenGitShell` and `Init`) since most commands are bound to be executed on a Cider/acre project.\\
 y←⍕y
 (namespace folder)←'' ''
 :If (,'.')≡,y
     folder←U.NormalizeFolder⊃1 ⎕NPARTS''
 :Else
     (list type)←U.GetOpenProjects
     :If 0=≢y
         :If 0=≢list
             :Return
         :ElseIf 1=≢list
             (namespace folder)←2↑list[1;]
         :Else
             (namespace folder)←2↑type U.SelectProject list
         :EndIf
     :Else
         :If ∨/'/\:'∊y
             folder←y
             :If 1=+/bool←(F.EnforceSlash¨list[;2])≡¨⊂F.EnforceSlash{⍵↓⍨-'/\'∊⍨¯1↑⍵}folder
                 namespace←⊃list[bool⍳1;]
             :EndIf
         :Else
             'Is not a fully qualified namespace name'U.Assert(⊃y)∊'#⎕'
             'There are no open Cider projects'U.Assert 0<≢list
             bool←list[;1]≡¨⊂y
             'Is not an opened Cider project'U.Assert 1=+/bool
             (namespace folder)←2↑list[bool⍳1;]
         :EndIf
         'Folder does not exist'U.Assert ⎕NEXISTS folder
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 folder←U.NormalizeFolder folder
⍝Done
